The function uses a series of if/elif statements to handle different units. If the string contains the character 'K', the value is multiplied by 1000 (because 1024 bytes is equal to 1 KiB). If the string contains the character 'M', the value is multiplied by 1000000 (because 1024 bytes is equal to 1 MiB). If the string contains the character 'G', the value is multiplied by 1000000000 (because 1024 bytes is equal to 1 GiB).

